From aedf5dba69f607429f81f6c07964e73b1662e4a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mytochondria audit <audit@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:30:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix strand handling for GTF features with undefined strand
 ('.')

A GTF exon line whose strand column is '.' gives the transcript (GTF.cpp:138-143)
and the gene (exonGeTrInfo.tab) strand code 0, distinct from 1 ('+') and
2 ('-').  Transcriptome_geneCountsAddAlign.cpp:32 handles code 0 explicitly --
"genes w/o strand will accept reads from both strands" -- but the transcriptome
BAM and the STARsolo counting paths tested only for code 1 and treated
everything else, code 0 included, as the minus strand:

* Transcriptome_quantAlign.cpp:107 set the transcriptomic alignment strand to
  1-aG.Str for a strandless transcript, so every record in
  Aligned.toTranscriptome.out.bam carried the opposite FLAG 0x10 to the one its
  SEQ implies.  The record was internally inconsistent: SEQ no longer matched
  the transcript at the reported POS, and a strand-aware quantifier
  (RSEM --forward-prob, salmon/eXpress) read every sense read as antisense.
* Transcriptome_classifyAlign.cpp:208, Transcriptome_geneFullAlignOverlap.cpp:24
  and :43, and Transcriptome_geneFullAlignOverlap_ExonOverIntron.cpp:30 rejected
  every read on a strandless gene under --soloStrand Forward (and accepted only
  antisense reads under Reverse), so such genes got zero counts in the Gene,
  GeneFull and GeneFull_Ex50pAS matrices.
* Transcriptome_alignExonOverlap.cpp:58 compared against trStr[tr1]-1, which is
  -1 for code 0, so no read ever matched a strandless transcript.

Strandless transcripts are now treated as '+' in the transcriptome BAM and
accept reads from both strands in the STARsolo counting paths, matching what
--quantMode GeneCounts has always done.  Genomic alignment, SJ.out.tab,
ReadsPerGene.out.tab and Log.final.out are unchanged, and annotations in which
every feature carries '+' or '-' (GENCODE, Ensembl, RefSeq) are unaffected.

Regression test: extras/tests/scripts/testStrandlessTranscript.sh maps the same
reads against two annotations that differ only in the strand column and requires
the transcriptome records and the STARsolo counts to be identical.  It fails on
2.7.11b (transcriptome FLAGs 0/16 swapped; STARsolo Gene/GeneFull/GeneFull_Ex50pAS
4 with '+' and 0 with '.') and passes with this change.
---
